# ============================================================================
#  NEVER COMMIT — private competition data
# ============================================================================
# The 2025 labels and the 2026 surprise holdout are the entire basis of the
# competition. If these reach the remote, Round 1, Round 2 and the holdout
# reveal are all ruined, and no re-run can fix it.
#
# This is the ONE rule in this file that is not about tidiness. The folders
# below are regenerated locally from yfinance by `organizer/prepare_data.py`;
# nothing in them needs a backup, because a backup of them is the disaster.
organizer/private/
*.csv.private

# ============================================================================
#  Run artefacts — regenerated by the documented commands
# ============================================================================
# Results embed the private 2025/2026 evaluation: per-day predictions and,
# in the *_paper files, equity curves that are cumulative products of the
# realised (private) returns. Derived from the private set, so they stay home.
# Rebuild with: evaluate.py, paper_trading.py, leaderboard.py (§4 of
# organizer/README.md).
organizer/results/
organizer/results/_sandbox/

# Participant submissions: untrusted executable Python. Never run them from a
# shared or CI host, and never commit a cohort's real submissions to a remote
# the organiser does not fully control.
organizer/submissions/

# ============================================================================
#  Machine / tooling noise
# ============================================================================
# AppleDouble sidecars. These reappear every time the repo is touched from a
# non-macOS filesystem — the working copy lives on an external SSD, and three
# of them kept landing inside participant/, where they would have shipped.
.DS_Store
._*
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Thumbs.db

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Agent/editor workspace state — not part of the workshop materials.
.zcode/
.vscode/
.idea/
